            {text:`She has no budget and needs to remove background noise from interview recordings.`, options:[`a paid DAW subscription`,`Canva`,`Audacity`], answer:2, fb:`Audacity is free, open source and has noise reduction. Canva is not an audio editor.`},
            {text:`She needs a logo that will print on T-shirts and appear on a website.`, options:[`a video editor`,`a raster photo editor only`,`a vector tool such as Inkscape`], answer:2, fb:`Vector tools produce scalable logos suitable for print and web.`},
            {text:`Her group of three needs to edit the proposal at the same time from home.`, options:[`a USB drive`,`a printed copy`,`a cloud collaboration tool such as Google Docs`], answer:2, fb:`Cloud collaboration allows real-time co-editing from different locations.`},
            {text:`Before building her app, she wants users to click through the screens and give feedback.`, options:[`an audio editor`,`a spreadsheet`,`a prototyping tool such as Figma`], answer:2, fb:`App prototyping tools create clickable mock-ups for audience testing.`},
            {text:`Which stage should come straight after writing the creative brief?`, options:[`publishing`,`analytics`,`planning and storyboarding`], answer:2, fb:`After the brief, you plan and storyboard. Publishing and analytics come much later.`}
