          up: {"title":"What do they have in common? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","q":"Audacity, Blender and Firefox are open-source software. A popular mobile game is also free to download. Which statement BEST explains why the free game is NOT open-source software?","options":[{"t":"It is not open source because it was made by a company rather than by volunteers.","fb":"Companies publish open-source software too, such as the open-source core of Android. Who made it does not decide."},{"t":"Its source code is not published under a licence that lets users study, modify and share it; a zero price alone does not make software open.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Open source is defined by the licence and access to the code, not by the price. Free-of-charge software with secret code is freeware."},{"t":"It is open source, because anyone can download it free of charge.","fb":"Free of cost is not the same as free to modify and share."},{"t":"It cannot be open source because it is a game; open source applies only to tools.","fb":"Many games are open source. The type of software does not decide it; the licence does."}]}
